// GLM-5.2 (llama.cpp / UD-Q5_K_XL) OpenCode provider snippet
// feat-2-glm-5.2-onprem-deployment, Task 2.6
//
// This is NOT a complete opencode.jsonc -- it is the "provider" entry to
// merge into an EXISTING opencode.jsonc on a DIFFERENT system than sys0
// (the Dell 7960T this feature deploys to). Paste the object below into
// that file's top-level "provider" object, alongside any other providers
// already there (e.g. "abacus", "ollama-sys0"), and replace <sys0-LAN-IP>
// with sys0's actual LAN address reachable from that other system (the
// same host/IP already used for that system's "ollama-sys0" entry, just a
// different port).
//
// Prerequisites (see this feature's Task 2.3/2.4 -- NOT done yet as of
// 2026-08-20): the llama.cpp GLM-5.2 systemd --user service on sys0
// (bin/08-llama-glm-5.2.service) must be installed AND started
// (`systemctl --user start llama-glm-5.2`) before this endpoint responds.
// Until then, http://<sys0-LAN-IP>:8092/v1 simply refuses connections.
//
// Model id `glm-5.2:UD-Q5_K_XL` matches the `--alias` flag added to
// bin/08-llama-glm-5.2.service -- without that alias, llama-server would
// instead report its own identity as the raw absolute GGUF file path in
// /v1/models and in every response's "model" field (confirmed empirically
// from an early spike response; see bin/08-llama-glm-5.2.service's header
// comment for the evidence).
//
// `limit.context: 768000` matches Task 2.3's decided production context
// size (768K, not the 896K candidate still flagged for revisit -- see the
// feature README's Decisions Made). `limit.output: 32768` is a reasonable
// placeholder cap, not a measured value -- adjust once real usage patterns
// are known (GLM-5.2's reasoning mode can consume a lot of tokens on
// `reasoning_content` alone).
//
// Known open item (Task 3.2, Phase 3): there is currently no confirmed way
// to drive GLM-5.2's --chat-template-kwargs reasoning-mode toggles
// (reasoning_effort: max/high, or enable_thinking: false -- REQ-004) from
// an OpenCode session through opencode.jsonc alone. Until Task 3.2
// resolves that, sessions through this provider run GLM-5.2 in its default
// mode (reasoning_effort: max, per unsloth's defaults) -- explicit
// low/no-thinking-mode testing happens via direct curl/API calls instead
// (Task 2.4/ACC-004).
//
// If OpenCode errors on a missing API key, add "apiKey": "not-needed"
// under "options" below -- REQ-008 means this endpoint has no real auth,
// but the AI SDK's openai-compatible provider may still want a non-empty
// placeholder string.

{
        "llama-cpp-sys0": {
            "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
            "name": "llama.cpp GLM-5.2 (SYS0)",
            "options": {
                "baseURL": "http://sys0:8092/v1"
            },
            "models": {
                "glm-5.2:UD-Q5_K_XL": {
                    "name": "GLM-5.2 (UD-Q5_K_XL)",
                    "limit": {
                        "context": 768000,
                        "output": 65536
                    }
                }
            }
        }
}
